  "term": "acetylcholinesterase inhibitor",
  "definition": "An acetylcholinesterase inhibitor is a substance that blocks the enzyme acetylcholinesterase, which normally breaks down acetylcholine in the synaptic cleft. This causes acetylcholine to remain active longer and at higher levels.",
